            <ArticleTitle>The pseudotumor cerebri syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>363-96</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ncl.2014.01.001</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0733-8619(14)00002-4</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The pseudotumor cerebri syndrome may be idiopathic or arise from a secondary cause. The major morbidity is visual loss, which may be severe and permanent. This article reviews the diagnosis, evaluation, and management of patients with pseudotumor cerebri syndrome in adults and children.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright © 2014 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
